  "clues": {
    "kinetics": "Food lowers early concentrations without changing overall exposure. It is 99% protein bound and cleared mainly through CYP3A metabolism.",
    "substance": "A white to off-white solid, practically insoluble in water, with a molecular weight of 473.39 g/mol.",
    "product": "Approved under an NDA in a single 50 mg tablet strength. The first dose is 100 mg, and the second dose is 50 mg.",
    "safety": "No boxed warning; contraindicated with strong CYP3A inhibitors. Pruritus and muscle spasms are the most common adverse reactions compared with placebo.",
    "indication": "Moderate to severe acute pain, including postoperative pain, in adults.",
    "mechanism": "A selective blocker of the NaV1.8 voltage-gated sodium channel in peripheral sensory neurons, which stops pain signals reaching the spinal cord and brain."
  },
  "tell": "A selective NaV1.8 blocker whose major active metabolite, M6-SUZ, is 3.7-fold less potent than the parent.",
